  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers return for the weekend. \n\nA weak surface low will track just north of the region late \nFriday through Sunday. A slow moving cold front will cross the \narea during the weekend, bring the risk of showers and \nthunderstorms. A southerly flow ahead of the front will advect \nmoisture into the region through the day Friday and into the \nweekend. PWATS of 1.5\" to 1.75\" inches will provide a moist \natmosphere. This moist air mass combined with forcing from the \nweak cold front and a shortwave trough crossing the area will \ngenerate periodic showers and thunderstorms. Some storms will \nhave the potential for heavy downpours at times, along with the \npotential for gusty winds. Showers may become better organized \nand steady for a period of time Saturday as a weak secondary \nsurface low tracks along the slow moving cold front. While WPC \nhas a Marginal Risk for excessive rainfall Saturday, with recent\nantecedent conditions, rainfall for the weekend is not expected\nto cause hydro issues.",
